# StyleX styles generation rules

- Use named imports.
- Name the variable containing the created styles like the component that uses them followed by 'Styles', like 'ComponentStyles'.
- Apply the styles (the '{...props()}' syntax) before any other attribute on the styled elements.
- Put the styles right below the component that is using them.

## Example

```TypeScript
import { create, props } from 'stylex';

function Component() {
    return <div {...props(ComponentStyles.base)} {/* other props go here, after the styles */}></div>
};

// styles below the component that uses them
const ComponentStyles = create({
    base: {
        color: '#00000';
    }
});
